.TH WB\-VIEW 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-view \- show what a session of a role sees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR view <issue> (<role> [\-\-in | \-\-out] | <path>)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Show what a session of a role will see, before it starts. wb view <issue> <role> prints the paths of its view, one to a line, the list the start makes the view from, and nothing else.
.PP
wb view <issue> <path> says for each role whether the path, from the root, is in its view: in, with the list and the line of the issue's file that hold it, or out, and why. A path named as a role is written ./<path>.
.PP
The level and the line view: are in wb prompt <role> <issue> \-\-stamp. It writes nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-in [<folder>]
Print what of HEAD the view holds in the folder (the root when none is given), one level deep: each file in it, and <count><tab><folder>/ for each folder below it.
.TP
.B \-\-out
Print the same for what the view leaves out. A folder is a path from the root, with or without a closing /.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The path is in the view of a role, or the view is shown.
.TP
.B 1
The path is in none, the folder is not in HEAD, or the issue has no accepted, committed file.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly (a file given as the folder too) or the repository is not set up.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wb (1) ,
